---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What battery standard does the Middle East use?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The Middle East predominantly uses JIS N-series batteries (N150/N200, models 145G51/190H52) for Japanese and Korean heavy trucks, with DIN/EN batteries (DIN88/DIN100) also common on European vehicles. Match the standard to the vehicle, not the region alone."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why does hot climate matter for truck batteries in the Gulf?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Heat accelerates lead-acid ageing and increases water loss in flooded batteries. High ambient temperatures shorten service life and raise self-discharge, so a robust thick-plate construction and correct electrolyte care are important in Gulf conditions."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What certifications do Middle East markets require?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Many Gulf markets require product conformity marking such as the GCC mark, with Gulf-standard import documentation. Requirements vary by country, so confirm the current certification and labelling rules with your importer before shipping."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you supply batteries to the Middle East?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. DINWEY exports JIS N150/N200 and DIN heavy-duty batteries to distributors across the Middle East, with batch CCA test data and full shipping documentation on every delivery."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Truck Batteries for the Middle East — DINWEY OEM"
  description="Heavy-duty truck batteries for Middle East distributors — hot-climate JIS/DIN construction and GCC-ready documentation. OEM supply from Chengguang Power Tech."
  jsonLd={faqJsonLd}
>
  <div class="container section">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#55606e;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <a href="/" style="color:#1e5aa8;">Home</a> &rsaquo; Markets &rsaquo; Middle East
    </nav>
    <h1 style="color:#0f1f3d;">Truck Batteries for the Middle East Market</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The Middle East is a core JIS market — Japanese and Korean heavy trucks dominate, running
      JIS N150/N200 batteries — with European vehicles calling for DIN88/DIN100 alongside them.
      DINWEY stocks both, with hot-climate construction and complete shipping documentation.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Key Takeaways</h2>
    <ol class="takeaways-list">
      <li><strong>Two standards run side by side</strong> — JIS N150/N200 for Japanese/Korean trucks, DIN88/DIN100 for European vehicles; match the battery to the vehicle, not the region alone.</li>
      <li><strong>Heat is the primary stress</strong> — high ambient temperatures accelerate lead-acid ageing and water loss, so thick-plate construction and disciplined electrolyte care matter in Gulf duty.</li>
      <li><strong>Documentation drives trade</strong> — distributors repeatedly value batch CCA test data and complete shipping paperwork, which DINWEY ships on every order.</li>
      <li><strong>Certification varies by country</strong> — Gulf markets commonly require conformity marking; confirm current rules with your importer before shipping.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Battery Standards for the Region</h2>
    <p>
      Pick the standard by the vehicle. Japanese and Korean heavy trucks — the backbone of Gulf
      fleets — take JIS N-series batteries in model codes N150 (145G51) and N200 (190H52). European
      commercial vehicles from MAN, Scania, Volvo and Mercedes take DIN/EN batteries in codes
      DIN88 (58827) and DIN100 (60038). DINWEY stocks both families so a distributor can cover a
      mixed fleet from one source.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Vehicle origin</th><th>Standard</th><th>DINWEY models</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Japanese / Korean heavy trucks</td><td>JIS</td><td>N150 (145G51) 900A CCA · N200 (190H52) 1100A CCA</td></tr>
        <tr><td>European commercial vehicles</td><td>DIN/EN</td><td>DIN88 (58827) · DIN100 (60038)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Hot-Climate Considerations</h2>
    <p>
      Heat is harder on a lead-acid battery than cold. High ambient temperatures speed up the
      chemical reactions that age plates and increase electrolyte water loss in flooded designs.
      The practical consequences: shorter service life, faster self-discharge while a vehicle sits,
      and — for flooded batteries — a greater need for electrolyte checks. DINWEY's heavy-duty
      thick-plate (Pb-Sb) construction is built to hold up under this duty, and AGM versions are
      available where fleets prefer a sealed, maintenance-free option.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Import &amp; Compliance</h2>
    <p>
      Many Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) markets require product conformity marking and
      Gulf-standard import documentation. Rules and labelling evolve, so treat the numbers as
      indicative and confirm the current certification and tariff position with your importer or
      freight forwarder before each shipment.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Product Lines for the Region</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:16px;">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>JIS Heavy-Duty (N150/N200)</h3>
        <p>145G51 and 190H52 for Japanese/Korean trucks — the region's core battery.</p>
        <a href="/products/jis-heavy-duty/">View JIS Heavy-Duty →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>DIN Heavy-Duty (DIN88/DIN100)</h3>
        <p>European-standard batteries for MAN, Scania, Volvo and Mercedes fleets.</p>
        <a href="/products/din-heavy-duty/">View DIN Heavy-Duty →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What battery standard does the Middle East use?</h3>
      <p>The Middle East predominantly uses JIS N-series batteries (N150/N200, models 145G51/190H52) for Japanese and Korean heavy trucks, with DIN/EN batteries (DIN88/DIN100) also common on European vehicles. Match the standard to the vehicle, not the region alone.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Why does hot climate matter for truck batteries in the Gulf?</h3>
      <p>Heat accelerates lead-acid ageing and increases water loss in flooded batteries. High ambient temperatures shorten service life and raise self-discharge, so a robust thick-plate construction and correct electrolyte care are important in Gulf conditions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What certifications do Middle East markets require?</h3>
      <p>Many Gulf markets require product conformity marking such as the GCC mark, with Gulf-standard import documentation. Requirements vary by country, so confirm the current certification and labelling rules with your importer before shipping.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Do you supply batteries to the Middle East?</h3>
      <p>Yes. DINWEY exports JIS N150/N200 and DIN heavy-duty batteries to distributors across the Middle East, with batch CCA test data and full shipping documentation on every delivery.</p>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:24px;">
      📚 Read more: <a href="https://docs.dinweysbattery.com/jis-vs-din-vs-bci/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JIS vs DIN vs BCI Standards</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
